==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wargod Kaihime '''at level 10.

Evolves into '''Immortal Kaihime''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Cleansing Flame Kaihime''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Narita Kaihime's DPS (including the [[Savage Blow]] chance) and range are quite high, allowing her to be used as a second [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]]. Sadly, there are plenty of units who, with more knockbacks or a lower cost, can take her place as general attacker. When it comes to her abilities, it is noteworthy that Narita can pose a good threat to Zombies with her high health and damage, but her high cost limits her there, while the opposite happens with Darks, where she can be afforded easily, but her sluggish attack speed and lack of knockbacks prevent her from leaving a big impact most of the time, as she is likely to be overran in between attacks.

What hurts this unit the most is the competition, as [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] will often be enough to crowd-control [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies, while the ability to slow will be made less and less important for [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]], leaving Narita's role against them to be that of an attacker, role that she won't perform well against mid-late game zombies due to her inability to reposition.

==='''True Form'''===
Immortal Kaihime's health increase will rarely come into play, while her effective DPS, increased by about 15% through better Savage Blow chance, will still not be enough to bring her to the same level as the better generalists. With this being said, it's still important to notice that Narita's health can unlock brand new uses for her, meaning that she could, potentially, become a very powerful asset in stages that feature waves that can hardly be blocked or long distance attacks that would easily interrupt and quickly kill other Ubers, allowing her to be quite useful in stages that feature [[Kory]], [[Dolphina]], [[Bore Jr.|Bore Jr]] or similar enemies, such as [[No Return Flights]].

==='''Ultra Form'''===
Cleansing Flame Kaihime gains more than just an awesome new look. As for less impactful changes, the 12.5% HP Buff and range increase from 440 to 455 both help emphasize Kaihime's already high survivability, with the latter letting her outrange specific backliners like [[THE SLOTH]]/[[Master A.]]. Cleansing Flame Kaihime also sees her speed doubled from 5 to 10, which simply allows her to reach the frontlines in a more timely manner.

However, her biggest buffs by far are in the damage department. With her Savage Blow chance increasing from 25% to 30%, and more importantly, gaining a 50% chance to create an [[Explosion]], Cleansing Flame Kaihime ends up with an absurd 21.7k DPS. This is without even mentioning how her attacks can pierce up to 733 range thanks to said Explosions, which distinguish her from other generic backliners like [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]] even outside of raw DPS. On Kaihime specifically, [[Sage Slayer]] is most useful for the enormous stat buffs it grants, giving her 26k EDPS and 460.8K EHP against all Sages. There's also the perk of it bypassing the debuff resistance of [[Oldstrich]] and [[Dark Dober]], where she can maintain her usual Slow uptime of ~52% (and Weaken if you unlocked that Talent). This is basically a death sentence for a majority of Sages. Overall, a useful Ultra Form should you choose to unlock it, but do be wary of the [[Catseye|Dark Catseye]] and massive Evolution costs.

==='''Talents'''===
Kaihime's talents are all fine, but nothing exceptional. '''[[Weaken]]''' has a low proc chance, only 40%, but has a good 75% uptime when it does proc at max. '''[[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]]''' can be helpful in mixed stages or stages with a [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]]. '''Cost Down''' can reduce her relatively high cost from 5250¢ to a far more manageable 4050¢, though it isn't a high priority. Finally, it has the typical stat Talents, which are worth investing if you use her for her stats, especially with her Ultra Form. However, remember to invest your Catseyes first if you really use her that much.

